# D[concurrent-terms]: `[execution] term_streams`, without a device. The
# program of a GPU run of the dipeptide in water, after
# md-exec-assign-streams: with TERMS the loops over tuples of an ordinary
# step are marked for the third stream and stand before the loop over
# pairs, which runs before the join; RECIPROCAL marks the reciprocal sums
# alone, SINGLE nothing; TERMS in the deterministic mode is RECIPROCAL; a
# loop over tuples that shares the destination of the pairs stays unmarked.
# `mdir check` states the resolution; an unknown value is refused.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- end/p' %S/term-streams-gpu.test | sed '1d;$d' | sed 's|INPUTS|%S/Inputs/dipeptide|' | sed -e 's/PRECISION/mixed/' > %t/template.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's/STREAMS/TERMS/' -e 's/DETERMINISTIC/false/' %t/template.toml > %t/terms.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's/STREAMS/RECIPROCAL/' -e 's/DETERMINISTIC/false/' %t/template.toml > %t/reciprocal.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's/STREAMS/SINGLE/' -e 's/DETERMINISTIC/false/' %t/template.toml > %t/single.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's/STREAMS/TERMS/' -e 's/DETERMINISTIC/true/' %t/template.toml > %t/deterministic.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's/STREAMS/BOTH/' -e 's/DETERMINISTIC/false/' %t/template.toml > %t/bad.toml
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_PRINT_AFTER=md-exec-assign-streams mdir emit terms.toml --stage=lowered 2> terms.mlir > /dev/null
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_PRINT_AFTER=md-exec-assign-streams mdir emit reciprocal.toml --stage=lowered 2> reciprocal.mlir > /dev/null
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_PRINT_AFTER=md-exec-assign-streams mdir emit single.toml --stage=lowered 2> single.mlir > /dev/null
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_PRINT_AFTER=md-exec-assign-streams mdir emit deterministic.toml --stage=lowered 2> deterministic.mlir > /dev/null
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_term_streams_ir.py %t/terms.mlir TERMS | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TERMS
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_term_streams_ir.py %t/reciprocal.mlir RECIPROCAL | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RECIPROCAL
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_term_streams_ir.py %t/single.mlir SINGLE | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SINGLE
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_term_streams_ir.py %t/deterministic.mlir RECIPROCAL | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RECIPROCAL
# RUN: not %python %S/Inputs/check_term_streams_ir.py %t/reciprocal.mlir TERMS
# Without destinations of their own the tuples cannot pass the pairs: the
# pass puts them back, unmarked.
# RUN: cd %t && mdir emit single.toml --stage=pipeline | sed 's/md-exec-assign-streams,/md-exec-assign-streams{reciprocal=true tuples=true},/' > shared.pipeline
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_PRINT_AFTER=md-exec-assign-streams sh -c 'MDIR_PIPELINE="$(cat shared.pipeline)" mdir emit single.toml --stage=lowered' 2> shared.mlir > /dev/null
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_term_streams_ir.py %t/shared.mlir RECIPROCAL | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RECIPROCAL
# RUN: cd %t && mdir check terms.toml | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHECK-TERMS
# RUN: cd %t && mdir check deterministic.toml | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHECK-DET
# RUN: cd %t && not mdir check bad.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BAD
# RUN: rm -rf %t
# TERMS: TERMS: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} loops over tuples on the third stream, {{[1-9][0-9]*}} beside a loop over pairs before a join and the kick
# RECIPROCAL: RECIPROCAL: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} reciprocal sums marked, no loop over tuples
# SINGLE: SINGLE: no op is marked and there is no join
# CHECK-TERMS: term_streams TERMS (as requested)
# CHECK-DET: term_streams RECIPROCAL (the deterministic mode keeps the tuples with the pairs)
# BAD: expected one of SINGLE, RECIPROCAL, TERMS for 'term_streams', got 'BOTH'
